      "riskNotes": "2026-08-21 critical re-audit v2 replaces the previous council lineup. Seteth now performs a readable folio handoff, Rhea receives it, and the end frame turns the authority away from the students. / Rhea too villainous, Seteth too old",
      "videoPrompt": "# Shot003 Seedance Prompt\n\nTarget: Seedance image-to-video, 10.3 seconds, cinematic live-action cathedral drama, 16:9.\n\nUpload exactly three images and label them START, KEY, and END. Use only those uploaded frames as hard anchors for identity, academy wardrobe, cathedral floor, altar axis, eyelines, and blocking. Do not replace the cast or add a named character.\n\nThe council meets inside the cathedral immediately after the wet monastery entrance. The visible named cast is Rhea, mature academy Seteth, female academy Byleth, and Dimitri. Seteth must read as the mature green-haired academy adviser from the uploaded frames, not a young generic man and not a war-phase redesign. Female Byleth is the only Byleth and remains an adult woman with teal-blue hair and dark professor coat. Keep everyone physically integrated into the same stone floor, light, depth, and perspective.\n0-2.6s: Begin on START. The heavy doors settle behind female Byleth and Dimitri as they take two quiet steps into the lower cathedral. Rhea remains above on the altar steps. Seteth holds a closed report folio beside her. Their attention pulls the students upward; no one faces the camera in a lineup.\n2.6-6.3s: Travel toward KEY along the aisle. Seteth takes two measured steps down and across, closes the folio firmly, then extends it to Rhea. Rhea raises one hand and accepts the folio. This transfer is the action peak. Byleth and Dimitri remain below, making small eye and posture reactions.\n6.3-9.45s: Hold the handoff long enough to read the institutional exchange. Rhea speaks calmly in Japanese: 西方教会が、ガスパール領主ロナートを扇動し、兵を挙げさせました。 Keep the line synchronized to the folio entering her hand; no theatrical villain performance.\n9.45-10.3s: Move into END. Rhea turns away toward the altar with the folio. Seteth steps laterally down the stair with his hands now empty. Dimitri turns toward an off-screen Ashe cue while female Byleth stays in left profile. Leave an empty aisle between the students and the authority for the next shot.\n\nUse restrained live-action timing, real foot contact, robe and folio weight, cathedral reverb, and a motivated dolly. No subtitles, captions, readable text, UI, Chinese or Mandarin voiceover. Reject if Seteth becomes young, if Byleth becomes male, if the folio never changes hands, if the cast becomes pasted cutouts, if the students form a line, or if START/KEY/END collapse into one council still.\n\n## Audio lock\n\nAll spoken dialogue in this shot must be Japanese only, using the exact Japanese line(s) already specified by the shot beat. Do not generate Chinese or Mandarin voiceover. Do not burn in subtitles, captions, dialogue boxes, or readable text.\n<!-- EP03_EXECUTION_CONTRACT_ADDENDUM_2026-08-24 -->\n\n## Canonical Execution Contract Addendum\n\nThis addendum normalizes the upload contract without changing the existing shot design. The model receives only the uploaded START, KEY, and END images at generation time.\n\n## Shot ID\n\nShot ID: Shot003\n\n## Duration\n\nDuration: 10.3 seconds.\n\n## Input Frames\n\n- start_frame: uploaded START image; begin from the visible Shot003 pre-action state.\n- key_frame: uploaded KEY image; reach the visible action/emotional peak without redesigning the shot.\n- end_frame: uploaded END image; settle on the visible handoff state for the next shot.\n- Preserve the current integrated live-action frames, shared scale, feet, contact shadows, wardrobe, and screen direction.\n\n## Motion\n\nAnimate the existing Shot003 action from START through KEY to END: Follow the existing shot-local Motion and Scene Beat sections above exactly. Use the uploaded START/KEY/END progression as the only action authority; do not import an older queue action or redesign the beat. Every change must be physical and visible; do not replace the chain with a lighting-only, crop-only, or frozen transition.\nKeep listed props and weapons attached to the responsible performer, keep unlisted people out, and hold the final state long enough to make the cut readable.\n\n## Camera\n\nUse the established live-action camera intent: Follow the existing shot-local Camera section above exactly. Preserve the uploaded axis, screen direction, location geography (cathedral), and depth relationships. Do not spin, mirror, or hide the action peak.\n\n## Performance\n\nKeep every named performer visibly present in the uploaded frames grounded through breath, eyeline, posture, hand contact, weight transfer, and restrained facial acting. Preserve the uploaded identity, academy/phase, gender presentation, wardrobe, face, hair, and weapon identity; do not add a performer from an older queue entry.\n\n## Audio\n\nJapanese spoken dialogue only for the exact line(s) already present in this shot's Audio section; preserve the environmental sound already specified. No Chinese/Mandarin voiceover and no burned-in subtitles or readable text.\n\n## Dialogue Timing / Delivery\n\n- `line_id`: `DL-EP03-003-1`; Rhea owns the exact Japanese line already declared in the shot Audio section.\n- Shot-local speech window: 3.92-9.43s; speech_seconds: 5.51s; listener reaction ends at 10.25s.\n- `speaker_handoff`: Rhea speaks once while the visible action continues; other listed performers listen and do not invent a reply.\n- `single_continuous_utterance`: speak the exact Japanese line once, continuously, without paraphrase.\n- `repeat_policy`: no repeat, no echo, no stutter, no restart, no second take.\n- `speech_end_cut_timing`: let the final syllable settle before the documented reaction/action handoff at 10.25s.\n\n## Continuity Locks\n\n- Receive the visible state in the uploaded START and hand the visible END state to the next shot; do not depend on unavailable filesystem or previous-shot context.\n- Preserve identity, wardrobe, props, weather/light, floor contact, screen direction, relative distance, and emotional/action state across all three anchors.\n- The model must animate the uploaded frames rather than invent a new location, cast member, costume, weapon, or story beat.\n\n## Reject If\n\n- START, KEY, and END collapse into one pose, a lighting-only variant, a lineup, a game screenshot, or pasted/cutout plates.\n- any named identity, gender presentation, age/phase, costume, weapon, screen direction, or floor contact drifts.\n- Chinese/Mandarin speech, subtitles, captions, UI, watermarks, borders, black frames, duplicate performers, or unlisted named characters appear.\n- the motion invents a new attack, reply, prop, camera axis, or next-shot handoff not supported by the uploaded frames.\n",
