      "riskNotes": "Reboard v1: the nearer guard advances toward Ashe, Catherine enters from the left and redirects that guard's long weapon, while the second guard retreats and Lonato remains separated. The beat is enter, take the lane, brace; it is not a direct attack on Lonato. / Catherine bypasses the guard line, the guards vanish, or the frame jumps directly to Lonato contact",
      "videoPrompt": "# Shot027 Video Prompt\n\n## Upload-only contract\n\nUpload exactly three integrated live-action images and label them START, KEY, and END. Use only those uploaded images as hard anchors for identity, wardrobe, terrain, screen direction, weapon state, and distance. Do not use screenshots, game images, local paths, or external references at run time.\n\n## Shot ID / Duration\n\nShot027. 5.5 seconds, 16:9.\n\n## Current frame set\n\nUse `manga_readability_reboard_v1_2026-09-09` as the current START/KEY/END set. The old critical re-audit sets are historical evidence only.\n\n## Story function\n\nThe nearer guard moves first. Catherine answers the actual pressure on Ashe before Lonato is touched. She enters from the left, redirects the guard's long weapon, and takes the half-step that will later make Lonato's protective crossing necessary.\n\n### START / pressure enters\n\nAshe remains near-right with one lowered nocked arrow. The nearer rebel guard has stepped toward Ashe through the opening, long weapon angled across the lane. The second guard braces behind him and keeps the route covered. Catherine's left shoulder and Thunderbrand enter from the left fog layer. Lonato remains separated uphill-left, shield coming up but not yet in contact with anyone.\n\n### KEY / guard redirected\n\nCatherine uses one short, grounded movement to catch and redirect the nearer guard's long weapon with the guard/flat of the gold serrated Thunderbrand. Her feet and hips show the leverage; the weapon is moved aside, not passed through a body. Ashe does not fire. The second guard begins a lateral retreat and Lonato watches the retreating guard from beyond the lane.\n\n### END / Catherine owns the lane\n\nCatherine settles in the cleared half-step in a low defensive guard. The nearer guard is displaced behind the barrier; the second guard is retreating toward Lonato. Ashe stays behind the line with the arrow lowered and nocked. Lonato remains untouched and separated, but the retreating guard is now visibly on his side of the field. This is the handoff into Shot028.\n\n## Motion / action grammar\n\n- 0.0-1.2s: inherit Ashe's restraint; the nearer guard creates pressure and Catherine breaks through the left edge.\n- 1.2-3.5s: Catherine redirects one long weapon with real footwork and takes the half-step.\n- 3.5-5.5s: the guard pair separates and retreats; Catherine braces in the cleared lane while Lonato sees the exposed guard.\n\nOne intervention only. Use wet-footed weight, armor drag, cloak movement, practical metal, and clear weapon paths. No flying, glow, magic beam, instant disarm, arrow release, or direct Lonato attack.\n\n## Camera / performance\n\nOpen in a side three-quarter geography view with Ashe, both guards, Catherine's entry, and Lonato's far direction. Track Catherine within the same axis; do not jump to a Lonato close-up. The focal signal is the advancing guard weapon meeting Catherine's grounded redirect. Catherine is economical and responsible, Ashe is held by conscience, the guards are frightened but active, and Lonato is forced to decide whether to protect the retreat.\n\n## Audio\n\nNo spoken dialogue. Use wet footfalls, one practical metal redirection, shield hardware, Ashe's held breath, and fog room tone. No Chinese/Mandarin voiceover, subtitles, captions, dialogue boxes, or readable text.\n\n## Continuity locks\n\n- Receive Shot026's lowered nocked arrow, right-side Ashe mark, left entry gap, two guard positions, and uphill-left Lonato direction.\n- Preserve the same guard pair; the nearer guard is the first threat and the second guard is the retreating handoff.\n- Hand Shot028 Catherine's low guard, Lonato's shield-led concern, the retreating guard, the cleared lane, and the same side axis.\n\n## Reject if\n\nReject if Catherine bypasses the guard, appears behind Lonato, flies, glows, attacks a body, or holds two weapons; if the guards disappear or duplicate; if Ashe fires; if Lonato is already hit or disarmed; or if the frame becomes a game screenshot, 3D render, anime image, poster lineup, pasted cutout, UI, border, subtitle, watermark, or repeated pose.\n\n<!-- EP03_EXECUTION_CONTRACT_ADDENDUM_2026-09-09 -->\n\n## Canonical Execution Contract Addendum\n\nThis addendum fixes the upload contract without changing the shot design. The model receives only the uploaded START, KEY, and END images at generation time.\n\n## Shot ID\n\nShot ID: Shot027\n\n## Duration\n\nDuration: 5.5 seconds.\n\n## Input Frames\n\n- start_frame: uploaded START image; begin from the visible guard pressure and Catherine's left-edge entry.\n- key_frame: uploaded KEY image; reach the visible weapon-level redirect.\n- end_frame: uploaded END image; settle on Catherine's cleared-lane defensive guard and the retreating second guard.\n- Treat the uploaded triptych as the only identity, wardrobe, terrain, distance, weapon-state, and screen-direction authority.\n\n## Motion\n\nAnimate the existing Shot027 action from START through KEY to END exactly as written above. The nearer guard creates pressure, Catherine takes one grounded step and redirects one long weapon, then the guard pair separates and retreats. Use one intervention only; every change must be physical and visible. Do not substitute a teleport, instant disarm, glow, impact montage, or frozen pose.\n\n## Camera\n\nFollow the existing side three-quarter geography camera on the same axis. Keep Ashe, both guards, Catherine's entry, her Thunderbrand, and Lonato's far direction readable together. Track the intervention without jumping to a Lonato close-up, spinning, mirroring, or hiding the weapon path.\n\n## Performance\n\nKeep Catherine grounded through foot leverage, hip rotation, hand contact, and restrained recovery. The nearer guard resists and is displaced; the second guard retreats; Ashe holds the lowered nocked arrow; Lonato watches without being attacked. Preserve the uploaded academy identity, face, hair, wardrobe, armor, and one Thunderbrand. No named performer is added, removed, or duplicated.\n\n## Audio\n\nNo spoken dialogue. Use only wet footfalls, one practical metal redirection, shield hardware, Ashe's held breath, and fog room tone. No Chinese or Mandarin voiceover, subtitles, captions, dialogue boxes, or readable text.\n\n## Dialogue Timing / Delivery\n\n- `dialogue_mode`: silent; no spoken dialogue, narration, or voiceover.\n- `line_id`: none; the intervention is carried by physical action and environmental audio.\n- `single_continuous_utterance`: not applicable; no speech is generated.\n- `repeat_policy`: no repeat, no echo, no stutter, no restart, and no invented reply.\n- `speech_end_cut_timing`: no speech end; preserve the metal-and-breath tail and cut on Catherine's cleared-lane handoff.\n\n## Continuity Locks\n\n- Receive Shot026's lowered nocked arrow, right-side Ashe mark, left entry gap, two guard positions, and uphill-left Lonato direction through the uploaded START.\n- Preserve the nearer guard as the first threat and the second guard as the retreating handoff; Catherine carries one Thunderbrand only.\n- Hand Shot028 Catherine's low guard, the retreating guard, Lonato's shield-led concern, and the cleared lane on the same side axis.\n\n## Reject If\n\n- START, KEY, and END collapse into one pose, a lighting-only variant, a lineup, a game screenshot, or pasted/cutout plates.\n- Catherine bypasses the guard, flies, glows, teleports, attacks Lonato, holds two weapons, or hides the contact point; Ashe fires; the guard pair duplicates or vanishes.\n- Chinese/Mandarin speech, subtitles, captions, UI, watermark, border, extra performer, body collision, blood, gore, face drift, costume drift, or weapon drift appears.\n",
