      "riskNotes": "Reboard v1: receive the dropped sword and upright imbalance, then let Lonato catch himself on one knee while female Byleth, Dimitri, and Ashe hold three separate distant marks. The empty lane and witnesses' restraint carry the moral consequence. / witnesses rush Lonato, the group forms a row, or the aftermath becomes a celebratory victory pose",
      "videoPrompt": "# Shot029 Video Prompt\n\n## Upload-only contract\n\nUpload exactly three integrated live-action images and label them START, KEY, and END. Use only those uploaded images as hard anchors for identity, wardrobe, terrain, screen direction, weapon state, and distance. Do not use screenshots, game images, local paths, or external references at run time.\n\n## Shot ID / Duration\n\nShot029. 6 seconds, 16:9.\n\n## Current frame set\n\nUse `manga_readability_reboard_v1_2026-09-09` as the current START/KEY/END set. The old critical re-audit sets are historical evidence only.\n\n## Story function\n\nThe disarm lands as a human consequence, not a victory tableau. Receive the dropped ordinary sword and Lonato's standing imbalance. He catches himself on his shield and settles to one knee while female Byleth, Dimitri, and Ashe hold their distance.\n\n### START / imbalance received\n\nLonato is still upright but his near knee has begun to buckle. The ordinary sword from Shot028 lies in the foreground mud. Catherine has exited. Dimitri holds a lateral safety mark several metres away; Ashe is farther back with bow lowered; female academy Byleth is in the rear layer with the Sword of the Creator lowered. The group is staggered, never a row.\n\n### KEY / shield catches the fall\n\nLonato catches himself with the shield and left hand; one knee makes physical contact with the muddy road. The sword stays abandoned in the foreground. Dimitri takes only a half-step to hold the side lane. Ashe lowers the bow and female Byleth remains rear. No one touches Lonato or raises a weapon.\n\n### END / quiet aftermath\n\nWiden slightly without resetting the geography. Lonato is fully kneeling and isolated by open mud and fog. The sword remains foreground. Dimitri, Ashe, and female Byleth stay in three separate depth layers, outside sword range. Catherine does not return. The silence and distance are the final change.\n\n## Motion / action grammar\n\n- 0.0-1.4s: inherit the dropped sword and Lonato's upright imbalance.\n- 1.4-3.6s: Lonato lowers one knee and catches himself with shield and hand; armor meets mud.\n- 3.6-6.0s: the camera widens a fraction; Dimitri holds, Ashe lowers, and female Byleth remains still in the rear.\n\nNo new strike, body contact, raised bow, raised lance, execution pose, celebration, duplicated Lonato, or frozen lineup.\n\n## Camera / performance\n\nKeep the same uphill-left road axis. Start as a medium continuation where the sword and buckling knee read together, then widen just enough to reveal the witnesses' restraint. Lonato's movement is exhaustion and surrender, not a theatrical bow. Dimitri is protective without attacking, Ashe is shaken but composed, and female Byleth is the only Byleth identity allowed.\n\n## Audio\n\nNo spoken dialogue. Use armor and knee meeting mud, one controlled Ashe breath, wet wind, distant fighting receding, and room tone. No Chinese/Mandarin voiceover, subtitles, captions, dialogue boxes, or readable text.\n\n## Continuity locks\n\n- Receive Shot028's dropped ordinary sword, Lonato's upright twisted balance, Catherine's exit, and the same muddy lane.\n- Use female academy Byleth only; no male or ambiguous Byleth variant.\n- Hand Shot030 a widened, non-celebratory aftermath with Lonato isolated and the three witnesses still separated.\n\n## Reject if\n\nReject if Lonato is already fully kneeling in START, remains standing at END, the sword disappears, two Lonato figures appear, male Byleth appears, Catherine returns, Dimitri or Ashe rushes or attacks, a bow or lance is raised, the group forms a row, or the image becomes a game screenshot, 3D render, anime image, poster lineup, pasted cutout, UI, border, subtitle, watermark, or repeated pose.\n\n<!-- EP03_EXECUTION_CONTRACT_ADDENDUM_2026-09-09 -->\n\n## Canonical Execution Contract Addendum\n\nThis addendum fixes the upload contract without changing the shot design. The model receives only the uploaded START, KEY, and END images at generation time.\n\n## Shot ID\n\nShot ID: Shot029\n\n## Duration\n\nDuration: 6.0 seconds.\n\n## Input Frames\n\n- start_frame: uploaded START image; begin from the visible dropped sword and upright imbalance.\n- key_frame: uploaded KEY image; reach the visible shield catch and one-knee contact.\n- end_frame: uploaded END image; settle on the visible full kneel and separated witnesses.\n- Treat the uploaded triptych as the only identity, wardrobe, terrain, distance, weapon-state, and screen-direction authority.\n\n## Motion\n\nAnimate the existing Shot029 action from START through KEY to END exactly as written above. Lonato receives the dropped sword, catches himself with shield and hand, lowers one knee into mud, and settles. Dimitri holds, Ashe lowers, and female Byleth remains in the rear. Every transition must be physical and visible; do not substitute a collapse without cause, a victory pose, a new strike, a frozen lineup, or a crop-only change.\n\n## Camera\n\nFollow the same uphill-left road axis as a medium continuation, then widen only enough to reveal the three witnesses' restraint. Keep the sword and buckling knee readable together. Do not spin, mirror, push into an execution close-up, or reset the geography.\n\n## Performance\n\nKeep Lonato grounded through armor weight, shield support, hand contact, knee-to-mud contact, and exhausted breath. Dimitri remains protective without attacking; Ashe lowers the bow; female Byleth remains the only Byleth identity and stays rear. Preserve the uploaded academy identity, face, hair, wardrobe, shield, ordinary sword location, and three separate witness layers. No named performer returns or duplicates.\n\n## Audio\n\nNo spoken dialogue. Use only armor and knee meeting mud, one controlled Ashe breath, wet wind, distant fighting receding, and room tone. No Chinese or Mandarin voiceover, subtitles, captions, dialogue boxes, or readable text.\n\n## Dialogue Timing / Delivery\n\n- `dialogue_mode`: silent; no spoken dialogue, narration, or voiceover.\n- `line_id`: none; the aftermath is carried by physical consequence and environmental audio.\n- `single_continuous_utterance`: not applicable; no speech is generated.\n- `repeat_policy`: no repeat, no echo, no stutter, no restart, and no invented reply.\n- `speech_end_cut_timing`: no speech end; preserve the armor-and-breath tail and cut on the widened non-rushing handoff to Shot030.\n\n## Continuity Locks\n\n- Receive Shot028's dropped ordinary sword, Lonato's upright twisted balance, Catherine's exit, and the same muddy lane through the uploaded START.\n- Use female academy Byleth only; no male or ambiguous Byleth variant. Keep Dimitri, Ashe, and Byleth outside sword range.\n- Hand Shot030 a widened, non-celebratory aftermath with Lonato isolated, sword foreground, and the three witnesses still separated.\n\n## Reject If\n\n- START, KEY, and END collapse into one pose, a lighting-only variant, a lineup, a game screenshot, or pasted/cutout plates.\n- Lonato is already kneeling in START, remains standing at END, the sword disappears, a second Lonato or male Byleth appears, Catherine returns, or any witness attacks or rushes.\n- Chinese/Mandarin speech, subtitles, captions, UI, watermark, border, extra performer, raised bow/lance, blood, gore, face drift, costume drift, or weapon drift appears.\n",
